      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "While the underlining problem is valid, and I myself am giving this an upvote. I do have some worries about the solution. Specifically, if it can't be toggled on/off. Or even give friends + select players permissions to see this.\nEverything I say following would stop being a worry with a proper permission system in place for this.\nFirstly, because I worry while you aren't asking for people to be able to see parts of other people's menus. I feel like having a floating blank panel would lead to an influx of people assuming that they should be able to.\nAlong with other creepy information that seems weird to want like my fps, ping, and other stats that feel like they should stay client side. \nOr even just the idea of when someone's trying to report/kick/kick vote a user for a bad behavior it may be even easier for them to tell and attempt to crash any player digging into their menus.\nSeeing my quick-menu radical would break the immersion of when I'd pull out current emotes among my friends.\nIN ADDITION, A QUESTION(S)!!\nWould a menu-player x-ray be another option? Either in addition or instead of? Or would that just not be practical even with an opacity slider?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
